1
00:00:00,810 --> 00:00:04,870
A thousand years on a thousand heads,

2
00:00:04,890 --> 00:00:08,420
And nobody ever asks the hat.

3
00:00:11,970 --> 00:00:14,690
She sat down proud with a chin up high,

4
00:00:14,710 --> 00:00:16,670
Ice in her hair and frost in her eye.

5
00:00:16,690 --> 00:00:17,650
I barely touched down,

6
00:00:17,670 --> 00:00:18,970
Didn't need a look.

7
00:00:18,990 --> 00:00:19,630
"SLYTHERIN!"

8
00:00:19,650 --> 00:00:20,910
Read her like a book,

9
00:00:20,930 --> 00:00:22,890
Then came the boy with the messy hair.

10
00:00:22,910 --> 00:00:24,810
Knees all shaking on the wooden chair.

11
00:00:24,830 --> 00:00:25,830
I found him some green,

12
00:00:25,850 --> 00:00:27,450
A serpent's spark —

13
00:00:27,470 --> 00:00:27,890
He begged "not there!"

14
00:00:27,910 --> 00:00:30,620
Like a cry in the dark.

15
00:00:30,870 --> 00:00:32,250
One took a second,

16
00:00:32,270 --> 00:00:33,330
One took all night.

17
00:00:33,350 --> 00:00:35,250
One wanted distance, one wanted a fight.

18
00:00:35,270 --> 00:00:37,050
The lions went wild in the red and the gold,

19
00:00:37,070 --> 00:00:41,120
But the hat already knew how the tale would unfold.

20
00:00:42,650 --> 00:00:45,150
The hat knew, the hat knew,

21
00:00:45,170 --> 00:00:47,150
Saw the green in him,

22
00:00:47,170 --> 00:00:50,650
And the gold in her too.

23
00:00:50,670 --> 00:00:52,470
He begged not the snakes,

24
00:00:52,490 --> 00:00:55,250
Now he's sneaking out at three.

25
00:00:55,270 --> 00:00:59,690
Holding hands with a serpent by the willow tree,

26
00:00:59,710 --> 00:01:01,750
Took him four long years,

27
00:01:01,770 --> 00:01:03,650
Took me one short song,

28
00:01:03,670 --> 00:01:05,690
The hat knew, the hat knew,

29
00:01:05,710 --> 00:01:07,370
All along.

30
00:01:07,390 --> 00:01:11,120
Now I sit on a shelf in the headmaster's den,

31
00:01:11,790 --> 00:01:15,680
The portraits spill the tea again and again.

32
00:01:15,810 --> 00:01:18,210
She hexed him at breakfast,

33
00:01:18,230 --> 00:01:20,330
She healed him by noon.

34
00:01:20,350 --> 00:01:22,050
He walked her to the tower,

35
00:01:22,070 --> 00:01:24,490
Underneath the moon.

36
00:01:24,510 --> 00:01:28,470
My song's too long and the first-years starve.

37
00:01:28,490 --> 00:01:30,470
I've got no chill,

38
00:01:30,490 --> 00:01:32,770
But I've got some nerve.

39
00:01:32,790 --> 00:01:34,590
The hat chose violence.

40
00:01:34,610 --> 00:01:36,850
No, darling — fate.

41
00:01:36,870 --> 00:01:41,290
A lion and a serpent on the same dinner plate.

42
00:01:41,310 --> 00:01:45,350
Ravenclaw'd have written them a sixty-page review.

43
00:01:45,370 --> 00:01:48,710
Hufflepuff'd have baked a cake that said I'm proud of you.

44
00:01:48,730 --> 00:01:51,250
Gryffindor'd have charged right in,

45
00:01:51,270 --> 00:01:53,250
With a sword and not a plan.

46
00:01:53,270 --> 00:01:55,370
Slytherin'd have blackmailed them.

47
00:01:55,390 --> 00:01:56,910
And honestly, I'm a fan.

48
00:01:56,930 --> 00:01:59,030
The hat knew, the hat knew,

49
00:01:59,050 --> 00:02:01,290
Saw the green in him,

50
00:02:01,310 --> 00:02:04,550
And the gold in her too.

51
00:02:04,570 --> 00:02:06,350
He begged not the snakes,

52
00:02:06,370 --> 00:02:09,130
Now he's sneaking out at three.

53
00:02:09,150 --> 00:02:13,570
Holding hands with a serpent by the willow tree,

54
00:02:13,590 --> 00:02:15,630
Took him four long years,

55
00:02:15,650 --> 00:02:17,250
Took me one short song,

56
00:02:17,270 --> 00:02:21,400
The hat knew, the hat knew all along.

57
00:02:21,970 --> 00:02:25,510
I've been inside both your heads,

58
00:02:25,530 --> 00:02:29,810
Heard every word you never said.

59
00:02:29,830 --> 00:02:31,970
She's scared, she's not brave,

60
00:02:31,990 --> 00:02:34,550
He's scared, he's not good.

61
00:02:34,570 --> 00:02:39,120
Each holds the half that the other one should.

62
00:02:39,210 --> 00:02:41,690
I don't sort by blood.

63
00:02:41,710 --> 00:02:43,970
I don't sort by name.

64
00:02:43,990 --> 00:02:46,530
I sort by the heart.

65
00:02:46,550 --> 00:02:52,550
And your hearts are the same.

66
00:02:52,570 --> 00:02:55,910
The hat knew, the hat knew,

67
00:02:55,930 --> 00:03:01,350
A thousand years of heads never quite these two,

68
00:03:01,370 --> 00:03:03,310
One begged not the green,

69
00:03:03,330 --> 00:03:05,650
One wore it like a crown.

70
00:03:05,670 --> 00:03:09,270
Now the whole castle's whispering it,

71
00:03:09,290 --> 00:03:13,670
Up and down the school screaming "Hat, you're mad!"

72
00:03:13,690 --> 00:03:18,330
I'm the oldest wingman this place ever had!

73
00:03:18,350 --> 00:03:20,490
The hat knew, the hat knew,

74
00:03:20,510 --> 00:03:22,570
The hat knew, the hat knew,

75
00:03:22,590 --> 00:03:28,300
All along.

76
00:03:28,530 --> 00:03:33,460
He would have done well in Slytherin.

77
00:03:33,730 --> 00:03:36,500
He's doing very well with one.
